   "id": "sanhedrin.30a.19",
   "daf": "30a",
   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "גָּמְרוּ אֶת הַדָּבָר, הָיוּ מַכְנִיסִין כּוּ׳. לְמַאן? אִילֵימָא לְבַעֲלֵי דִינִין – הָתָם קָיְימִי! אֶלָּא לְעֵדִים.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that after the judges «finished the matter» and reached a decision, «they would bring» them «in.» The Gemara asks: «Whom» would they bring in? «If we say» they would bring in «the litigants,» this cannot be, as «they were there» the whole time; they never left the room. «Rather,» they would bring in «the witnesses.»"
  }
 ],
